The:lang()pseudo-class 
is used to select elements with a lang attribute with the specified value.

There are many more structural pseudo-classes available:

### Code Snippets

```
p:first-child
{
color: blue;
}

---

p em:first-child
{
color: blue;
}

---

p:first-child em
{
color: blue;
}

---

<html>
<head>
<style>
q:lang(no) {
quotes: "~" "~";
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<p>Some text <q lang="no">A quote in a paragraph</q> 
Some text.</p>
</body>
</html>
```
